  "description": "IWUXOQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C63 H70 Mn4 N3 O28 S3 Yb3,2(C2 H3 N1),3(C2 H6 O1). From the CIF bond table, Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Yb1 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.140-4.052 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.44-133.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C63H70Mn4N3O28S3Yb3·2(C2H3N)·3(C2H6O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
